<title>USA: U.S. House passes budget accord, sends to Senate.</title>
<headline>U.S. House passes budget accord, sends to Senate.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The House late Saturday passed and sent to the Senate a fiscal 1997 budget accord that grants President Clinton more funds for domestic programs and pays for Republicans' defense priorities.</p>
<p>The bill passed on a vote of 370 to 37 and is expected to be voted on in the Senate late Monday just hours before the Oct. 1 deadline for the start of the new fiscal year.</p>
</text>
